A||||12||Greg Piet||Disabling Stock Rev Limiter||||1||
Z||000000||Greg Piet||06-11-2001||03:52 PM||||Ok my 3.1 is installed and running GREAT!<BR>I am very happy with it!<BR>With my my cam selection, I was hitting my MSD rev limter @ 5700 when it was still pulling hard.<BR>I was thinking the motor should be OK at 6200 and would like to try revving aroung the 6000 RPM range.<P>How do I disable the stock 6 grand rev limiter?  If it is the PROM that needs to be modified?  If so where do I get one?  The stock PROM seems to be working peachy with the 3.1 so currently I am only concerned with disabling the stock rev limiter and using the MSD rev limiter exclusively.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA Region 72 Race Director<BR>#47 SM<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.physics.unlv.edu/~gregpiet/Jan1617s.jpg">    <BR>Our lady of blessed acceleration dont fail me now!||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||06-11-2001||04:17 PM||||What year? 1226869 ECM or 1227170 ECM?<P>Also, have you *hit* the limiter or do you just think it's there?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Greg Piet||06-11-2001||06:52 PM||||I have no idea what ECM # it is, but I blew my first motor by the gas pedal sticking and the ECM Rev limiter working but unfortunately the thing would rev above 6 grand because the rev limiter wasnt as good as the MSD one.<P>I am guessing the ECM # is on a sticker on the ECM?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jay||06-11-2001||06:57 PM||||Try this link:http://64.177.38.56/index.html and look for the reprogrammed chip, it removes speed and rev limiters and also changes the fuel curve.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Slammed Fiero||06-11-2001||07:00 PM||||88's have no rev limiter , get a chip from one , it's a direct replacement. I believe a fellow by the name of Joe Wyman sells them as a "performance chip" I would get an 88 chip and run a 6500rpm module from MSD. Fiero's are hard at autocrosses depending on the course, sometimes hunting for a gear. 1st is too high , 2nd is out of the powerband. Espically if you have removed the Cat converter.<P>I regularly run my 2.8 (basically stock) up to the 6200rpm fuel cut off at autocrosses and track events. I have friends who run the 88 chip in the earlier ECM along with an MSD 6AL set to 6700rpm for years with no problems (mild motor, stock rebuild with 1.6 rockers , stronger springs). As long as the valvetrain is strong (not stock) you should be fine.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">      <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.<p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 06-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Greg Piet||06-11-2001||08:25 PM||||oops I didnt mention I have an 85 Fiero...<BR>OK so who wants to give me an old stock 88 PROM that they dont need anymore?????<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I never find 88's at the boneyard  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||06-11-2001||11:24 PM||||85 is the 6869. 86-88 is the 7170. The 88 chip won't work in the 85 ECM. The 85's do have the limiters. The rev is set to 6000/4000. Later 85 updates had no speed limiter.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Greg Piet||06-12-2001||04:13 AM||||So where do I get a PROM to disable it?<BR>Possibly "JET" chip company?  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||84Bill||06-12-2001||01:41 PM||||Could it be valve float?||||reg||5
Z||000009||Greg Piet||06-12-2001||03:08 PM||||Bill...<BR>I mean no disrespect but what the heck are you talking about(honestly I am confused)????<BR>Are you saying there may be vlave float at 6000 which I am mistaking for a Rev limiter?<BR>I know that there is a Rev limiter stock in the PROM at 6000 and more people than terryk has confirmed this in older threads.<P>I do appreciate all posts so please dont take this the wrong way.||||reg||1
Z||000010||terryk||06-12-2001||04:21 PM||||The longer runners make these engines wheeze out above about 6000 with a better cam and springs.<P>But, if you'z gots 'ta rev it up there....||||reg||1
